### Page 1 of 2

```text
1

RESOLUTION NO. _______

ENTITLED:
“A
RESOLUTION DESIGNATING THE
ALLOCATION OF
WYOLOTTO REVENUES STATUORILY DEDICATED TO THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE BE DISTRIBUTED TO COMMUNITY RECREATION
AND EVENTS FOR THE PURPOSE OF CONSTRUCTION,
REMEDIATION, AND COMPLETION OF QUALITY OF LIFE
PROJECTS IN THE CITY OF CHEYENNE FOR A FIVE (5) YEAR
PERIOD.”

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne (“City”) recognizes the need for improvement
for Quality of Life amenities throughout the entire municipality; and

WHEREAS, pursuant to Wyoming Statute § 9-17-111(b) “Disposition of lottery
proceeds”, these monies shall be paid by the treasurer to the treasurers of the counties, cities and
towns for payment into their respective general funds; and

WHEREAS, the percentage of the balance that will be distributed to each city will be
determined by computing the percentage that sales of lottery tickets collected by retailers that
city to total sales of lottery tickets collected by retailers in all counties including their cities and
towns. This percentage of the monies shall be distributed to the City of Cheyenne relative to its
population within Laramie County; and

WHEREAS, the monies allocated from this resolution received from the WyoLotto
revenue to the City shall be used for the construction, remediation, and completion of, but
not limited to, projects deemed a high priority by the director of Community Recreation
and Events, or his or her designee, to be presented annually by resolution to the governing
body for consideration and appropriation; and

WHEREAS, the monies allocated from this resolution received from the WyoLotto
revenue to the City may be used for potential grant matches for the construction,
remediation, and completion of, but not limited to, projects deemed a high priority by the
director of Community Recreation and Events, or his or her designee, to be presented to
the governing body for consideration following standard operating procedures for
pursuing grant funding laid out by the City; and

WHEREAS, the monies allocated from this resolution received from the WyoLotto
revenue to the City may not be used to compensate for lost wages, payroll, or overtime
costs; and

WHEREAS, the monies allocated from this resolution received from the WyoLotto
revenue to the City may not be used to create new or update strategic plans, but are
intended to display tangible results to the community at large that quality of life projects
are being completed; and
By Alessandra at 9:27 am, Dec 13, 2021
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
2

WHEREAS, this resolution shall become effective beginning July 1, 2022 and shall
be deemed in effect for the period of five (5) years where the resolution will be
reconsidered for extension by the governing body.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the City of Cheyenne hereby designates
the allocation of WyoLotto revenues to the City of Cheyenne be distributed to Community
Recreation and Events for the purpose of construction, remediation, and completion of
quality of life projects in the City of Cheyenne for a period of five (5) years.

PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this ____ day of ______________, 2021.

_____________________________________

Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)
ATTEST:

________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
